# Fight an armoured monster long enough to check every term of the armour
# model: graded penetration of coverage, and subtractive damage (inc-b0w2).
#
# The subject is a cave ankylosaurus (lib/mon1.irh:4644): Arm 18, Def 10.
# Heavy armour behind a low Defense Class is what makes it the right subject.
# Natural armour sits behind NATURAL_COVERAGE, so the bar an attacker must
# clear to start turning it aside is 10 + 14 = 24, which a levelled barbarian
# reaches on a middling roll rather than never or always. Every roll from
# there up turns aside one more point, so one fight sweeps the whole ramp.
#
# It swings back for 3d6 blunt, which is the other half of the measurement:
# those blows meet the player's WORN armour behind the player's own Coverage,
# so a single fight exercises both bars and both buckets.
#
# The character is levelled to 7 first, in wizard mode, for two reasons. A
# level 1 barbarian dies to the second tail swipe, and barbarian natural armour
# does not arrive until 7th (lib/classes.irh:180) -- and a creature carrying BOTH
# natural armour and a worn suit is the only case where the two bars differ.
#
# The oracle is logs/armour.log, written by ArmourProbeNote in src/Fight.cpp
# under INCURSION_ARMOUR_PROBE. tools/check_armour_model.sh does the
# arithmetic on it. Nothing here reads the screen, so menu letters below the
# chargen prefix are the only fragile part.
#
# NOT covered: penetrating weapons (WT_PENETRATING), because nothing in the
# starting kit has the flag and wizard mode cannot add it. The arm*2/5 term
# is checked by inspection only. Say so rather than let the check imply it.
#
# Menu letters move when a list changes; run this at the seed its caller
# supplies and no other.

@include chargen.keys

# Into play. ESC until the arrival-room description is gone; "Afoot" is on the
# status panel and appears only once the map is up. This is the entry
# tools/keys/assassin-bard.keys uses, and it is proven.
@until "Afoot" ESC
@dump:inplay

w       # wizard mode
@expect "Enter wizard mode"
y       # "Enter wizard mode?" -- yes
w       # [w] Wizard Mode Switches
DOWN DOWN
SPACE   # Free Advancement: NO -> YES
ESC

# --- LEVEL TO 7 -----------------------------------------------------------
# The character sheet is a menu, so no game time passes while this happens.
d
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "You feel hardier" ESC
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "You feel hardier" ESC
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "You feel hardier" ESC
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "You feel hardier" ESC
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "You feel hardier" ESC
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "You feel hardier" ESC
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "You feel hardier" ESC
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "You feel hardier" ESC
@expect "Barbarian 7"
@dump:sheet     # the Coverage row and its breakdown; inc-vifx reads this
ESC     # back to the map

# --- THE FIGHT -------------------------------------------------------------
# Walk east, which is to attack whatever stands there. A summoned monster
# starts neutral, so the first blow needs confirming; from then on it is
# hostile and swings back, and those blows are what measure the player's WORN
# armour behind the player's own Coverage. One bout of this is enough: it
# yields around fifty resolved attacks, in both directions.
#
# The beast wins. That is expected and is not a failure -- 3d6 blunt against a
# barbarian 7 gets there in about ten exchanges, and every measurement this
# file exists for has already been written to logs/armour.log by then. The
# death prompt is answered so the session still ends cleanly.

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Dinosaur"
@choose "cave ankylosaurus"
RIGHT   # the location cursor starts on the player; one step east
ENTER
@dump:summoned

RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
SPACE SPACE
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
SPACE SPACE
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
SPACE SPACE
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
SPACE SPACE
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
SPACE SPACE
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
SPACE SPACE
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
SPACE SPACE
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
SPACE SPACE
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
SPACE SPACE
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
SPACE SPACE
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
SPACE SPACE
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
SPACE SPACE
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
SPACE SPACE
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
SPACE SPACE
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
SPACE SPACE
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
SPACE SPACE
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
SPACE SPACE
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
SPACE SPACE
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
SPACE SPACE
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
SPACE SPACE
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
SPACE SPACE
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
SPACE SPACE
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
SPACE SPACE
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
SPACE SPACE
@dump:fought
@while "Die?" y
SPACE SPACE SPACE
@quit
